{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\nPydantic AI 1.107 emits `pydantic_ai._warnings.PydanticAIDeprecationWarning` when `infer_model(\"openai:<model>\")` constructs a model: in v2 the ambiguous prefix will switch from Chat Completions to Responses. A pinned-environment runtime probe captured that exact category and message. Rebar currently relies on Chat Completions for hosted OpenAI and OpenAI-compatible endpoints, so leaving the ambiguous prefix would silently change the wire contract on upgrade. The operator approved preserving Chat Completions with `openai-chat:`; story `upbeat-illadvised-springtail` owns the eventual deliberate Responses migration.\n\n## Approach\nNormalize every rebar-composed or legacy `openai:` Pydantic AI model target to the explicit `openai-chat:` qualifier at the shared primary and model-class/fallback resolution seams. Update both independent ProviderSession gates: the cfg.base_url builder registration and the per-candidate endpoint-override guard must recognize `openai-chat`, so local OpenAI-compatible endpoints keep their provider/profile override. Preserve other provider qualifiers unchanged and document `openai-chat:` as the supported Chat Completions spelling.\n\n## Scope\n- Update `src/rebar/llm/anthropic_model.py` and `src/rebar/llm/model_classes.py` so inferred, explicitly qualified, primary, and fallback OpenAI targets resolve to `openai-chat:`.\n- Update both `openai`-keyed gates in `src/rebar/llm/providers.py`: cfg.base_url builder registration and the per-candidate endpoint-override guard.\n- Strengthen provider-resolution, custom-endpoint, fallback, and library-contract tests in `tests/unit/test_pydantic_ai_runner.py`, `tests/unit/test_openai_compatible_provider.py`, `tests/unit/test_provider_qualifier.py`, `tests/unit/test_model_classes.py`, and `tests/interfaces/store/test_llm_framework.py`.\n- Update canonical operator/developer examples in `.github/llm-providers/openai.toml`, `docs/llm-framework.md`, `docs/llm-example-configs.md`, `docs/workflow-authoring-v2.md`, `docs/reuse-surface.md`, the model examples in `src/rebar/llm/config.py` and `src/rebar/llm/capabilities.py`, and their packaged `src/rebar/schemas/workflow.v{1,2,3}.schema.json` descriptions.\n- Keep legacy `openai:` spellings in tests that explicitly prove backward-compatible normalization.\n- The nine `src/rebar/llm/eval_specs/*.eval.yaml` grader strings are out of scope: current `run_eval` executes only deterministic scorers and never constructs those report-only grader models, so they cannot emit this warning; the deliberate Responses migration story can revisit them if an executable judge path is added.\n\n## Testing\n- The held-out oracle imports `PydanticAIDeprecationWarning` from `pydantic_ai._warnings` and promotes it to error around real `infer_model` calls for inferred, explicit, custom-endpoint, and fallback paths. Before repair, `infer_model(\"openai:gpt-4o\")` was observed RED with the exact warning; after repair, every rebar-resolved target constructs without it.\n- Run real loopback custom-endpoint tests and provider/fallback parity tests to prove Chat Completions payloads, endpoint routing, and structured-output profile behavior are preserved.\n- Sweep the focused unit tests with the exact warning category promoted to error, then run repository lint and typecheck.\n- Search canonical examples for ambiguous `openai:` spellings while excluding intentional legacy-compatibility tests and report-only eval graders.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Inferred OpenAI targets resolve to `openai-chat:`; verified by provider-resolution tests.\n- [ ] Legacy-explicit `openai:` targets resolve to `openai-chat:`; verified by interface tests.\n- [ ] Primary and fallback model-class targets resolve to `openai-chat:`; verified by model-class tests.\n- [ ] Real model construction emits no `pydantic_ai._warnings.PydanticAIDeprecationWarning` with that exact category promoted to error.\n- [ ] Loopback custom endpoints still receive Chat Completions payloads; verified by real-seam provider tests.\n- [ ] The custom-endpoint profile override remains active on cfg.base_url and per-candidate endpoint paths.\n- [ ] Non-OpenAI targets and provider-conflict checks remain unchanged; verified by provider-parity tests.\n- [ ] Canonical operator and developer LLM examples use `openai-chat:` for Chat Completions.\n- [ ] Focused tests pass.\n- [ ] Repository lint passes.\n- [ ] Repository typecheck passes."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787049173278079001,"uuid":"0cf07bf5-dfc1-4c9b-b221-359c3d29fc78"}